== 3.9 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Which of the following is a macronutrient?],
  [nitrogen],
  [molybdenum],
  [boron],
  [zinc]
)

#mcq(2, [How many nutrients are regarded as essential for plant growth?],
  [twenty-four],
  [eight],
  [four],
  [sixteen]
)

#mcq(3, [Nitrogen is most important for],
  [seed hardness],
  [fruit colour],
  [root development],
  [leaf and stem growth and the green colour]
)

#mcq(4, [Phosphorus is most important for],
  [stem strength],
  [water uptake],
  [root development, flowering and seed formation],
  [leaf expansion]
)

#mcq(5, [Potassium is most important for],
  [stem strength, disease resistance and fruit quality],
  [chlorophyll formation],
  [nitrogen fixation],
  [root elongation]
)

#mcq(6, [Yellowing of the older leaves first is a symptom of the deficiency of],
  [boron],
  [nitrogen],
  [calcium],
  [iron]
)

#mcq(7, [Yellowing of the young leaves while the veins remain green suggests a shortage of],
  [iron],
  [potassium],
  [phosphorus],
  [nitrogen]
)

#mcq(8, [Magnesium is essential because it is part of the],
  [root cap],
  [chlorophyll molecule],
  [cell wall],
  [pollen tube]
)

#mcq(9, [A deficiency of boron is likely to show as],
  [purple stems],
  [hollow stem and poor fruit set],
  [scorched leaf edges],
  [yellow older leaves]
)

#mcq(10, [Farmyard manure improves the soil chiefly by],
  [supplying nitrogen instantly],
  [raising the pH sharply],
  [adding organic matter and improving structure],
  [killing soil organisms]
)

#mcq(11, [Poultry droppings should be composted before use because fresh droppings],
  [attract no insects],
  [have no effect on soil],
  [are too concentrated and can scorch seedlings],
  [contain no nitrogen]
)

#mcq(12, [Green manure is],
  [composted household waste],
  [a crop grown and ploughed in while still green],
  [fresh animal dung],
  [a chemical fertiliser]
)

#mcq(13, [Compost is ready for use when it is],
  [green and fibrous],
  [still hot in the middle],
  [dark, crumbly and smells of earth],
  [dry and powdery like ash]
)

#mcq(14, [Which practice is NOT part of making good compost?],
  [turning the heap regularly],
  [alternating dry and green layers],
  [keeping the heap damp],
  [keeping the heap dry and undisturbed]
)

#mcq(15, [The three figures on a bag of NPK 20-10-10 represent the percentages of],
  [N, P and K by weight of the bag],
  [N, P₂O₅ and K₂O],
  [lime, sulphur and magnesium],
  [moisture, ash and fibre]
)

#mcq(16, [A 50 kg bag of NPK 15-15-15 contains how much nitrogen?],
  [50 kg],
  [1.5 kg],
  [7.5 kg],
  [15 kg]
)

#mcq(17, [Urea contains about],
  [60 per cent potassium],
  [20 per cent nitrogen],
  [46 per cent phosphorus],
  [46 per cent nitrogen]
)

#mcq(18, [Single superphosphate supplies mainly],
  [potassium only],
  [nitrogen only],
  [magnesium only],
  [phosphorus, with calcium and sulphur]
)

#mcq(19, [A farmer needs 60 kg of N per hectare and has urea (46 per cent N). How much urea should he buy?],
  [about 130 kg],
  [about 276 kg],
  [about 46 kg],
  [about 60 kg]
)

#mcq(20, [Banding of fertiliser is preferred to broadcasting in a sandy soil because banding],
  [adds organic matter],
  [reduces leaching below the root zone],
  [increases the plant population],
  [raises the pH]
)

#mcq(21, [Fertiliser should not be applied to wet leaves because],
  [the salt concentration burns the leaf],
  [it improves absorption],
  [it kills weeds],
  [it prevents leaching]
)

#mcq(22, [Splitting the nitrogen application into two doses is done to],
  [increase the total quantity applied],
  [save on labour],
  [reduce leaching and volatilisation losses],
  [raise the soil pH]
)

#mcq(23, [Urea loses nitrogen to the air as ammonia chiefly when it is],
  [mixed with compost],
  [dissolved and injected],
  [worked into moist soil],
  [left on the surface in hot weather]
)

#mcq(24, [Which of these is a straight fertiliser?],
  [muriate of potash],
  [NPK 20-10-10],
  [NPK 15-15-15],
  [compound NPK 10-20-20]
)

#mcq(25, [Soil fertility is best defined as],
  [the depth of the topsoil],
  [the amount of water in the soil],
  [the number of earthworms present],
  [the ability of the soil to supply nutrients in available form]
)

#mcq(26, [A crop rotation that includes a legume improves fertility because the legume],
  [adds phosphorus to the soil],
  [raises the pH],
  [fixes atmospheric nitrogen in its root nodules],
  [uses no water]
)

#mcq(27, [Leaving land under bush fallow restores fertility mainly by],
  [returning organic matter and nutrients to the soil],
  [killing all soil organisms],
  [adding fertiliser free of charge],
  [raising the water table]
)

#mcq(28, [Liming an acid soil benefits the crop mainly because lime],
  [raises the pH and makes phosphorus available],
  [drains the field],
  [adds nitrogen to the soil],
  [kills weeds]
)

#mcq(29, [Sheet erosion is best described as],
  [the collapse of a stream bank],
  [the removal of a thin layer of soil over a whole slope],
  [wind removing fine particles],
  [deep channels cut into the field]
)

#mcq(30, [Gully erosion is controlled most directly by],
  [check dams and afforestation],
  [broadcasting fertiliser],
  [removing all vegetation],
  [deeper ploughing]
)

#mcq(31, [Mulching helps to control erosion because it],
  [increases runoff],
  [protects the surface from raindrop impact],
  [hardens the soil],
  [removes the topsoil]
)

#mcq(32, [Contour ploughing means ploughing],
  [only at the foot of the slope],
  [in a circle round the field],
  [across the slope along the contour],
  [up and down the slope]
)

#mcq(33, [Which of these is the correct order of a soil sampling procedure?],
  [take one core from the centre, then test it],
  [sample only the best corner of the field],
  [divide the field, take cores, mix them, quarter the heap],
  [quarter the field, plough it, then sample]
)

#mcq(34, [A composite soil sample is taken so that the laboratory result],
  [shows the deepest horizon],
  [represents the whole field],
  [reflects one weak spot in the field],
  [measures the rainfall]
)

#mcq(35, [Erosion is more severe on a field that is],
  [flat and covered],
  [bare, steep and long],
  [mulched and contoured],
  [under bush fallow]
)

#mcq(36, [Which of these is a micronutrient?],
  [copper],
  [magnesium],
  [sulphur],
  [calcium]
)

#mcq(37, [Organic manure is usually applied before ploughing because],
  [it must be mixed into the soil where roots will feed],
  [it is killed by light],
  [it floats on the surface],
  [it evaporates in the sun]
)

#mcq(38, [The main advantage of fertiliser over manure is that fertiliser],
  [improves soil structure],
  [supplies a known quantity of nutrient quickly],
  [is cheaper per hectare],
  [adds humus]
)

#mcq(39, [Which practice most directly conserves both soil moisture and soil fertility on a slope?],
  [burning the bush],
  [removing all crop residue],
  [deep ploughing up the slope],
  [terracing with a cover crop]
)

#mcq(40, [The nutrient whose deficiency shows as purple or reddish colouring of the stems and leaves is],
  [phosphorus],
  [nitrogen],
  [potassium],
  [calcium]
)

